  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.Ramachandran Nair vs Food Inspector on 26 September, 2018 Author: P.Ubaid Bench: P.Ubaid In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice P.Ubaid Wednesday, The 26Th Day Of September 2018 / 4Th Aswina, 1940 Crl.Rev.Pet.No. 2024 of 2006 Against The Order/Judgment In Cra 284/2004 of Addl. District Court (Adhoc), Kottayam Against The Order/Judgment In Cc 192/1997 of J.M.F.C.,Vaikom Revision Petitioner/Appellant/Accused: M.Ramachandran Nair, S/O. Madhavan Nair, Ajith Bhavan, Thalayolaparambu, Vaikom Taluk. By Advs. Sri.V.Rajendran (Perumbavoor) Sri.George Varghese Kizhakkambalam Respondents/Respondents/Complainant: 1 Food Inspector, Ettumanoor Circle, Ettumanoor. 2 State Of Kerala, Represented By Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam. Other Present: Sri.C.M.Kammappu(Sr.Public Prosecutor) This Criminal Revision Petition Having Been Finally Heard M.Ramachandran Nair vs Food Inspector on 26 September, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/160405846/ 1 On 26.09.2018, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: Crl.Rev.Pet.No. 2024 of 2006 -2- O R D E R",
    "facts": "The revision petitioner herein challenges the conviction and sentence against him under Section 16(1A)(i) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act (for short \"the PFA Act\"). He faced prosecution in the court below on the allegation that at about 1.00 p.m. on 02.04.1997, when the Food Inspector of the Ettumanoor Circle visited his grocery shop, he was found selling food articles without license under the PFA Act, and some quantity of dal purchased by the Food Inspector for consideration was found adulterated on analysis at the Regional Laboratory. 2. The prosecution examined five witnesses, and proved Exts.P1 to P20 documents in the trial court. On a claim of warranty made by the revision petitioner, the second accused was also impleaded during trial. 3. The accused denied the incriminating circumstances when examined under Section 313 Cr.P.C.. In defence, one witness was examined as DW1, and Ext.D1 was also proved. Now he is before this Court in revision. 6. When this revision petition came up for hearing, the learned counsel submitted that as regards the conviction under Section 16(1A)(i) of the PFA Act, the recent decision of the Honourable Supreme Court in PEPSICO case is applicable, and the accused will have to be acquitted.",
    "arguments": "7. In Pepsico India Holdings Pvt. Ltd. v. Food Inspector (2009 (1) KHC 983), the Honourable Supreme Court has held that in cases where the Central Government has not notified the laboratory for examination of food articles, and also the method of analysis for different items of food articles, the accused cannot be found guilty. The application of the Pepsico decision of the Honourable Supreme Court in the pending matters was considered by a Division Bench of this Court in Rasheed N.K. v. Food Inspector, Thalassery and Another (2016 (2) KHC 679 (DB)). This Court held that in cases involving adulterated food article for the analysis of which the Government of India has not M.Ramachandran Nair vs Food Inspector on 26 September, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/160405846/ 2 notified any method of analysis, or the laboratories for analysis, the accused will have to be acquitted.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "7. In Pepsico India Holdings Pvt. Ltd. v. Food Inspector (2009 (1) KHC 983), the Honourable Supreme Court has held that in cases where the Central Government has not notified the laboratory for examination of food articles, and also the method of analysis for different items of food articles, the accused cannot be found guilty. The application of the Pepsico decision of the Honourable Supreme Court in the pending matters was considered by a Division Bench of this Court in Rasheed N.K. v. Food Inspector, Thalassery and Another (2016 (2) KHC 679 (DB)). This Court held that in cases involving adulterated food article for the analysis of which the Government of India has not M.Ramachandran Nair vs Food Inspector on 26 September, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/160405846/ 2 notified any method of analysis, or the laboratories for analysis, the accused will have to be acquitted."
  },
